WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
We might already know what the One Piece&nbsp;
is and where is it hidden, because i found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:09.360
the X best theories about the big treasure Luffy&nbsp;
is trying to find in order to become pirate king.　

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.560
Starting with a theory that has actually&nbsp;
already been confirmed, in case you don’t know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:18.570
the only person that has ever discovered the&nbsp;
one piece so far was the former pirate king gol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:25.920
D roger on a island that is almost impossible to&nbsp;
reach and that most people don't even know about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.200
But if Roger discovered the One Piece first, who&nbsp;
put it there in the first place? There were tons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.660
of theories about this, until Eiichiro Oda,&nbsp;
the author of One Piece, confirmed that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:42.060
legendary One Piece treasure was created&nbsp;
by a mysterious character called Joy Boy.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.800
Joy Boy was a legendary character who lived&nbsp;
800 years ago who is still super mysterious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.140
but hugely important to the world of&nbsp;
One Piece. To find Joy Boy’s treasure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:57.000
the One Piece, Roger had to read these&nbsp;
ancient, nearly indecipherable artifacts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.940
called Poneglyphs. If a pirate can find all&nbsp;
4 of the Red “Road” Poneglyphs, the road to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.800
the final treasure will be unlocked.&nbsp;
After Roger found Joy Boy’s treasure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:14.040
he laughed uncontrollably, and the island that&nbsp;
held the treasure became known as “Laugh Tale”

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.900
So what is it?

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:21.540
Well this next theory says that **The&nbsp;
One Piece is the Devil Fruit Tree.**

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.560
The main power system in One&nbsp;
Piece are the devil fruits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:31.140
magical fruits that when eaten give a&nbsp;
person unbelievable powers. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.380
we still don’t know where these&nbsp;
devil fruits come from. How are they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:39.840
made? Where do they come from? Why is it that a&nbsp;
person who eats one is cursed to never swim again?

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.920
Someone who found such a treasure and&nbsp;
had access to tons and tons of super rare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.840
devil fruits could form a supremely&nbsp;
powerful crew. If an evil pirate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.700
such as Luffy’s main rival, Blackbeard, were&nbsp;
to find the tree that grew every devil fruit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.980
his crew would become nearly unstoppable as&nbsp;
he spread chaos and war throughout the world.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.500
We still have so many questions about&nbsp;
devil fruits, so maybe we’ll finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:21.120
get an answer at the end of the series.&nbsp;
Maybe Laugh Tale contains a giant tree&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.500
that grows the devil fruits. After all, the&nbsp;
devil fruits might not just be an awesome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.420
power system - they might be tied into&nbsp;
all of the complex history of the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:35.640
One Piece world. That would be crazy, but&nbsp;
a big theory that would be less crazy is…

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.920
that **The One Piece is Nothing**

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.260
Now, I know this sounds super anticlimactic -&nbsp;
but hear me out. Some fans think that when Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:49.440
finally reaches Laugh Tale, he’ll open a treasure&nbsp;
chest to reveal…nothing at all. If this were true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:55.020
fans the world over would descend upon&nbsp;
the Internet overflowing with pure rage.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.520
However, people who predict that the One&nbsp;
Piece might be nothing at all have some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.580
solid evidence to support their theory.&nbsp;
All the way back in the East Blue Saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:11.460
on the Island of Rare Animals, the early members&nbsp;
of the crew met a character named Gaimon.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.720
While almost every part of the East Blue&nbsp;
Saga serves to set up the larger story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:21.660
the Gaimon arc - which is really just&nbsp;
a single chapter - feels a bit out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:25.980
place. Everywhere else, we gain a crew&nbsp;
mate or meet an antagonist who still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:31.980
plays a role in the story. However, Gaimon’s&nbsp;
chapter just seems like a random side quest.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.740
Gaimon is a man with a large bushy&nbsp;
green afro who sought a treasure at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:41.940
the top of a high cliff. However, after&nbsp;
falling during his climb to the top,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:47.940
he landed and became permanently lodged inside&nbsp;
a treasure chest. After waiting for 20 years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:55.140
Luffy investigates the treasure at the top of the&nbsp;
cliff…only to find five empty treasure chests.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:58.560
Given that Gaimon and Luffy have a lengthy&nbsp;
conversation in the chapter about the One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.720
Piece treasure as a whole, could this be&nbsp;
foreshadowing for the end of the series as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:10.800
a whole? Did Oda hide the answer to the One Piece&nbsp;
in plain sight all the way back in Chapter 22?

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:16.980
Gaimon’s real treasure wasn’t gold. It was&nbsp;
his hope. It was his dream. In the same way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:22.500
the pirates of the One Piece world have set to&nbsp;
the sea in pursuit of their dreams - a life of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:28.560
adventure is a worthy endeavor regardless&nbsp;
of any tangible outcome in the end. Gaimon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.580
despite not becoming rich, became the&nbsp;
guardian and friend of the rare animals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:37.020
on his island. But if there are clues&nbsp;
for that at the beginning of the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:42.960
then something that seems more likely given the&nbsp;
HUGE reveals Oda’s been dropping lately is that…

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:43.140
**The**&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.060
****************************************************************One&nbsp;
Piece is the Ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:45.720
Kingdom****************************************************************

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:50.820
On the other side of things, the One Piece&nbsp;
treasure may be the remains of the Ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:55.680
Kingdom. We still don’t know a lot about the&nbsp;
Ancient Kingdom - we don’t even know its name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.320
but what we do know is that the Ancient Kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.060
was an advanced civilization&nbsp;
that lived over 800 years ago.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:13.440
The organization that controls the One Piece&nbsp;
world known as the World Government originated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:19.020
as 40 nations who came together to overthrow&nbsp;
the Ancient Kingdom. After the Ancient Kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:22.920
was destroyed, the World Government&nbsp;
erased the history of its existence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:27.300
They completely destroyed all traces of an&nbsp;
entire century called the “Void Century.”

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:33.180
However, if the One Piece ends up being the&nbsp;
remains of this ancient kingdom, then the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:38.400
history will finally be revealed. The characters&nbsp;
will learn all there is to know about the Ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.680
Kingdom, Joy Boy, and the Void Century. And it&nbsp;
will finally be revealed how the World Government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:50.280
took power in the first place and what their true&nbsp;
ambitions are. This would set us up perfectly for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:56.280
a final battle against the World Government. And&nbsp;
while that does seem like an awesome final battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:02.280
maybe the treasure is something that more&nbsp;
lines up with the themes of the story. Such as…

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:05.940
**The** **One Piece is the&nbsp;
friends they made along the way**

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:10.920
The idea that One Piece is the adventure itself&nbsp;
or all the friends Luffy made along the way is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:19.620
another big theory. This one is very similar to&nbsp;
the idea that the One Piece is “nothing” as well.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:25.200
And while it would be disappointing,&nbsp;
this theory has some valid evidence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:30.720
too. The biggest evidence for this theory&nbsp;
comes from an arc called Sabaody Archipelago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:34.680
when Silvers Rayleigh, the 1st mate&nbsp;
of the pirate king Gol D. Roger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:41.160
straight up offered to spoil the end of the story.&nbsp;
Rayleigh, who would later become Luffy’s mentor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:46.680
told the crew that he could tell them all&nbsp;
about the secrets of the One Piece. Usopp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:52.200
was all too ready to hear the truth of the&nbsp;
great treasure, but Luffy quickly shut him up.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:58.860
To Luffy, finding the treasure had no worth at&nbsp;
all if he took a shortcut. To him the thrill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:05.880
of adventure, the journey itself, is just as&nbsp;
worthy as any physical treasure he could obtain.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:13.440
After all, no matter what the One Piece is,&nbsp;
some fans will probably be disappointed in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:18.780
the end result. But whatever lies at the&nbsp;
end of the Grand Line doesn’t erase how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:24.240
much joy we’ve had as fans in getting to know&nbsp;
these characters and following their story.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:28.560
However, there’s some good news for fans who&nbsp;
would be majorly disappointed if the One Piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:34.020
turned out to be nothing at all or adventure or&nbsp;
friendship. Eiichiro Oda has actually gone on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:42.240
record stating that the One Piece is a physical&nbsp;
treasure. Fans asked him directly if the One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:47.940
Piece would turn out to be the friends they made&nbsp;
along the way and he explicitly turned them down.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.600
Instead of becoming pirate king by&nbsp;
the way, my personal journey to reach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:57.360
1.000.000 subscribers this year seems&nbsp;
almost impossible and is only possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:01.500
with your help. So if you want to see&nbsp;
more of this type of content and want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:05.220
to be a part of this crazy journey of&nbsp;
ours, all you have to his subscribe.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.860
But if it’s not the friends we&nbsp;
made along the way, then maybe…

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.380
********************************************************The&nbsp;
One Piece is…One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:10.800
Piece********************************************************

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:19.200
As in, the One Piece is the actual story we’re&nbsp;
reading. Okay, now this one is crazy. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:23.700
my brain hurts a little just thinking&nbsp;
about it. But at the same time it’s one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:27.720
of the coolest theories out there.
Now, we don’t necessarily mean that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:33.120
Roger was just sitting on Laugh Tale reading&nbsp;
manga volumes. Maybe the epic tale that is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:38.700
One Piece story is written on the unbreakable&nbsp;
Poneglyphs that keep the historical record of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:43.620
the Ancient Kingdom. After all it seems like&nbsp;
a “tale” or story that makes Roger “laugh.”

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:48.600
Roger comments on the treasure saying that&nbsp;
he wishes he could have lived in Joy Boy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:53.580
time and that he was “too early” getting&nbsp;
to Laugh Tale for some mysterious reason.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:59.400
There’s actually a big prophecy that says&nbsp;
Joy Boy will return - and all hints point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:04.980
to Luffy being the reincarnation of&nbsp;
Joy Boy…whatever that exactly means.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:11.460
One Piece is a hilarious manga so it would&nbsp;
definitely make Roger laugh. In addition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:16.860
the narrator often sounds like they’re telling the&nbsp;
story from some future point, so perhaps someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:22.740
will write the story or add to the story that’s&nbsp;
already there and leave it on Laugh Tale. The One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:27.540
Piece treasure is likely something that can unite&nbsp;
the whole world, and nothing can bring people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:33.780
together like a great story. So maybe the story&nbsp;
of Luffy’s adventures, either through prophecy or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.780 --> 00:10:33.720
through some weird time travel stuff, is the One&nbsp;
Piece. And speaking of weird time travel stuff…

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:36.420
********************************************************The&nbsp;
One Piece is Time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.020
Travel********************************************************

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:39.540
We already know that a character named Toki ate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.780
the Time-Time fruit. This allows&nbsp;
her to jump forward in time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:49.620
but not backwards. What if the One Piece is&nbsp;
something that *can* travel backwards in time?

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:54.120
This is a very crazy idea, but what if&nbsp;
Luffy isn’t a reincarnation of Joy Boy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.120 --> 00:11:01.440
at all. What if he time travels back to the Void&nbsp;
Century and he’s actually the original Joy Boy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:04.980
too? After all with the introduction of the&nbsp;
character Toki and her devil fruit ability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:07.440
time travel is now a real power in the story.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:12.960
By going back and changing history, Luffy&nbsp;
could prevent all the suffering the World&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:16.380
Government caused throughout the&nbsp;
centuries instead of just making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:22.680
things better for people in the present.&nbsp;
That’s why Roger laughed at his story. Why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:29.160
he wished he could have met joy boy and&nbsp;
why he said that he was too early. Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:33.608
wasn’t born yet. But if that theory’s a bit&nbsp;
too crazy for you, here’s a more tame one:&nbsp;

00:11:33.608 --> 00:11:33.720
****************************************************************************************************************

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:37.260
**The One Piece is just a bunch of treasure**

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:42.720
Now we come to what most pirates in the&nbsp;
One Piece world *think* the One Piece is:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:50.700
a bunch of treasure. Gold, jewels, riches, and&nbsp;
valuables. You know, a stereotypical pirate horde.&nbsp;

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:56.400
And you can’t blame them for thinking this -&nbsp;
I mean, Roger has Gold in his name. His ship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:00.900
the “Oro” Jackson uses the&nbsp;
Spanish word for gold, “Oro.”

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:05.400
However, what the leagues of pirates who set&nbsp;
out to find his treasure fail to recognize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:11.700
is that Roger isn’t your typical pirate - his&nbsp;
treasure is almost certainly not just monetary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:16.560
especially now that we have seen Roger’s&nbsp;
reaction to Laugh Tale and received many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:21.660
hints about the Void Century, Joy Boy, and&nbsp;
the Ancient Kingdom. Much more likely is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:26.580
that Roger’s “treasure” is something related&nbsp;
to the great mysteries of the One Piece world.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:32.760
As disappointed as money-loving Nami will be if&nbsp;
she doesn’t find wealth beyond her imagination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:38.580
the fanbase certainly won’t be if it’s&nbsp;
something a lot deeper than that. And as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:44.400
hyped as Oda gets about this final reveal, even&nbsp;
stating the series will end once it’s revealed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:48.420
it just makes us more excited&nbsp;
to reach the finale. For years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:53.460
the fanbase assumed that finding the One Piece&nbsp;
would then set off the final war. The author’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:57.900
recent comments would suggest, though, that&nbsp;
finding the One Piece actually will mark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:05.400
the end of the series instead. Whatever it is,&nbsp;
Oda must imagine it will be quite the pay off.

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:09.900
**The One Piece is on the Moon**

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:14.820
Now we’re going to get into some wilder theories.&nbsp;
But the thing is: This is Oda we’re talking about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:22.500
Whatever the One Piece is is going to be wild. So&nbsp;
even though these ideas might seem out there at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:27.780
first, they’re probably a lot *more* likely&nbsp;
than the theories we’ve already gone over.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:32.700
Starting with: the One Piece is on&nbsp;
the Moon. I guess this is more about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:37.200
“where” the One Piece is than “what”&nbsp;
the One Piece is, but hear me out.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:45.180
There’s something going on with the Moon in One&nbsp;
Piece. The members of the mink race have powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:48.000
Sulong transformations that depend on it. They&nbsp;
can only transform into this form during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:52.740
full moon. On the island of Ohara, there&nbsp;
was a Celestial Model with seven moons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:58.740
The Sun God Nika is pictured jumping&nbsp;
in front of it. Lunarians, like King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:04.680
are named after it given the “Luna” in their&nbsp;
name. And most of all, we’ve seen from Enel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:12.600
one of Luffy’s former enemies from SKypiea,&nbsp;
go to the moon. Enel’s cover story shows that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:19.320
there are remains of a civilization on the moon&nbsp;
as well as space pirates and an army of robots.

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:23.760
Clearly the moon is going to play&nbsp;
a role in the story at some point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:28.620
so could it be that the reason Laugh&nbsp;
Tale is so elusive is because it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:33.060
been in outer space the whole time?&nbsp;
On the moon, Enel found ruins that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:38.160
seemed to depict the winged races of the One&nbsp;
Piece world as well as the ancient weapons.

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:42.000
If the Straw Hats end up there,&nbsp;
they could learn the full truth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:46.200
of the Ancient Kingdom and the Void&nbsp;
Century from the remnants of the Lunar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:50.880
Civilization - that truth itself could&nbsp;
very well be the One Piece. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:55.440
there are some other crazy locations&nbsp;
where the One Piece could be located:

00:14:57.180 --> 00:15:00.300
**********************************************One&nbsp;
Piece is in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.020
Whale**********************************************

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:05.400
Maybe one of the reasons it’s so hard for&nbsp;
pirates to find the One Piece is because it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:11.820
doesn’t stay in one place. This theory states&nbsp;
that the treasure is actually inside the belly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:16.080
of a giant whale. As mentioned earlier,&nbsp;
when the crew first entered the Grand Line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:21.300
the most dangerous sea in One Piece, their&nbsp;
ship was swallowed by the whale Laboon.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:25.080
Inside, they weren’t digested&nbsp;
thankfully. Instead they found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:30.840
themselves in a very pleasant environment,&nbsp;
as the Roger’s doctor Crocus had taken up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:35.760
living inside Laboon so that he could more&nbsp;
easily treat Laboon’s medical problems.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:41.340
What if the beginning of the Straw Hat crew’s&nbsp;
journey in the Grand Line is a mirror image of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:46.800
the end? What if once again they have to&nbsp;
go into the belly of a whale in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:58.740
find the One Piece treasure? But that’s not the&nbsp;
only place where the One Piece could be hiding:

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:03.060
**One Piece is beneath Enies Lobby**

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:06.480
During the Enies Lobby arc, the Straw&nbsp;
Hats take on the World Government at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:12.720
their main judicial center. Enies Lobby&nbsp;
is a very peculiar island. It is always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:16.080
day time there. And despite being&nbsp;
located in the middle of the ocean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:20.940
there is a massive hole in the middle of&nbsp;
the sea that Enies Lobby is built above.

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:27.060
What’s at the bottom of this hole? Where does it&nbsp;
go? Well, according to this theory it might just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:32.820
be the One Piece itself. After all, what better&nbsp;
way could the World Government prevent people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:39.420
from finding the treasure than building one of&nbsp;
their main bases right on top of it? After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:43.140
only the Straw Hats are insane enough&nbsp;
to launch an all out assault against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:52.800
this government island. But now let’s get&nbsp;
back to what the One Piece actually is:

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:58.980
**One Piece is Bink’s Sake**

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:01.680
This theory for the One Piece was&nbsp;
popularized by another YouTuber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:08.040
Artur, and it utilizes the fact that the lyrics&nbsp;
to Bink’s Sake seem to hold a lot of clues as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:13.020
to the truth of the One Piece. Bink’s Sake&nbsp;
is a popular song among pirates that Brook,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:17.520
the ship’s musician sings, when he’s first&nbsp;
recruited to the crew. The Bink’s Sake song&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:26.520
hints at the drums of liberation and the&nbsp;
coming of the Dawn - both ideas that keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:31.260
recurring throughout the story. So the song&nbsp;
also seems to be hinting at Joyboy’s return.

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:37.920
This theory also makes a guess at what&nbsp;
Luffy and Roger’s secret dream is. On Wano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:41.100
it’s revealed through Oden’s journal&nbsp;
and Ace’s conversations with Yamato,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:46.380
that both pirates share a secret dream&nbsp;
that for now is hidden from the audience.

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:52.800
One popular guess for this dream is that Luffy’s&nbsp;
dream is to throw a party where everyone in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:58.140
world is invited. After all, after every arc,&nbsp;
he loves to celebrate with a huge party. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:03.420
thinks everyone should be able to eat and drink&nbsp;
as much as they want and make “merry” so to speak.

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:08.760
Luffy’s dream to become a pirate in the first&nbsp;
place was inspired by Shanks’s celebrations at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:16.860
aptly named…Party’s Bar - which would make this&nbsp;
reveal foreshadowed in a way from chapter one.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:19.740
And what do you need to throw a&nbsp;
party for the whole world? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:25.860
you’re going to need a whole lot of sake.&nbsp;
Specifically, Bink’s Sake would be a jug of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:32.100
sake big enough that all the world could party&nbsp;
together - coming together as “one piece.”

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:37.320
And when we think of how important the exchange&nbsp;
of sake cups between Ace, Sabo, and Luffy is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:43.920
this giant party would be like Luffy - or Joyboy&nbsp;
- exchanging sake cups and becoming like family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:49.500
to everyone across the world’s oceans. And&nbsp;
speaking of joining the world’s oceans:

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:53.040
**One Piece is destroying the Red Line**

00:18:53.040 --> 00:19:01.080
This theory says that One Piece isn’t an object:&nbsp;
it’s an action. Specifically, the One Piece refers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:08.460
to joining the world’s oceans together into&nbsp;
“One Piece” by destroying the Red Line itself.

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:13.020
Currently the people of the world are&nbsp;
separated from each other and the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:31.800
way for them to travel elsewhere is to brave the&nbsp;
treacherous oceans. Not only would merging the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:38.220
seas together make the oceans into “One Piece”,&nbsp;
it would bring the world’s people together too.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:42.180
What’s the evidence for this being the One&nbsp;
Piece, though? Well, think back to the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:46.200
chapter after the Straw Hat crew entered the&nbsp;
Grand Line. When they met the whale Laboon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:51.180
what was he doing (other than eating their&nbsp;
ship)? Well, Laboon was repeatedly bashing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:55.740
his head against the Red Line, leaving it&nbsp;
covered in scars, in an effort to reunite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:55.740 --> 00:20:01.980
with his long lost crewmates - who we later found&nbsp;
out to be the ship’s skeleton musician, Brook.

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:12.840
Our next clue comes from the Fishman Island Arc&nbsp;
- which is exactly one half of the Grand Line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:16.920
away from Reverse Mountain. On Fishman&nbsp;
Island an accomplished fortune teller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:20.400
Madame Sharly, predicts that&nbsp;
Luffy will destroy Fishman Island.

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:29.220
The prediction doesn’t come true during the&nbsp;
arc, but she’s never missed a prediction yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:33.360
so Luffy likely will cause the&nbsp;
destruction of Fishman Island&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:37.500
before the end of the series. It just&nbsp;
so happens that the Red Line and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:42.120
World Government capital of Mariejois are&nbsp;
situated directly above Fishman Island.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:46.440
If he were to destroy Mariejois&nbsp;
and the entire Red Line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:50.220
it would collapse upon Fishman&nbsp;
Island destroying it. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:55.440
by making use of the giant ship the Noah, the&nbsp;
Fishmen might be able to finally make their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:59.880
home on the surface of the world instead&nbsp;
of being forced to live beneath the sea.

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.400
Destroying the Red Line would also help many of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:06.900
the Straw Hats fulfill their ultimate&nbsp;
dreams. If the seas were all combined,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:11.940
it would form the All Blue for Sanji. Brook&nbsp;
would be reunited with Laboon. Franky could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:16.680
freely voyage around the world and Nami&nbsp;
could reach any sea to draw her maps.

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:25.020
And this theory in particular has a lot&nbsp;
of evidence speaking for it. It’s a crazy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:30.900
story that involves Oars, Greek Mythology and&nbsp;
the true history of the one piece world. So I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:30.900 --> 00:21:36.180
really recommend you check that video&nbsp;
out right here. Thanks for watching.

